2026-10-06T16:35:21.203064Z DEBUG xai_acp_lib::gateway: sending "session/prompt" request: {"sessionId":"2adc838b-6005-4b74-8560-4f5dea735ab1","prompt":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform one independent READ-ONLY final review of AzGuard plan P4.9 decideMany. You are the requested native Grok4.7/high reviewer. Inspect the full completed scope listed in scope.json, the complete candidate.diff (includes all new files), its actual source files and affected dependencies/tests. No code edits, commands, new agents, external research, execution history, or unrelated plan migration. Return the verdict, actionable findings with file:line, concrete trigger/impact and proposed correction; no speculative style/extra-process findings. End with GREEN only if there are no acceptance-blocking findings; otherwise FINDINGS. State inspected coverage and meaningful residual limitations concisely.\n\nStart with candidate.diff and norms/item.json. Norms/09-authorization-semantics.md §§1/9/16, norms/14-verification.md V45/V64/V99/V120, norms/17-crm-acceptance-tests.md R58/R68, and D14/D15/D16 in norms/decisions.json define the contract. This is one core implementation item. Owner explicitly requests efficient affected-package checks, final whole-scope review, and Grok with NO context parameter; previous 500k routing requirements were removed. Public wrappers/visibility/list/count/EXPLAIN remain later items. Internal Authorizer API is tuple resolve(Model|SubjectRef, enum|string, ?panel) and decideMany(list<AccessRequest>, ?ActorRef):DecisionSet. Kernel DecisionSet/IdentityCodec frozen API remains unchanged.\n\nReview invariants: scalar parity incl scope/reason/state/actor, per-request business policies/restrictions/conditions and before/after (including prospective resource clones), one now, original order, unique subject/tenant groups with shared fence across <=100-scope chunks and whole retry (max3), dynamic Prepare/catalog + assignment coherence, errors isolated from unrelated grants groups/static PolicyOnly and BeforeDeny, cache refresh/absolute expiry/transaction authority, no premature observations of discarded attempts, no N+1 host structural/eligibility reads on 1k/10k CRM. Queryable definitions use fresh whereKey chunks and tenantOf; generic resolves once per unique ref. Eligibility must retain actual role/contribution field witness; external uses allowsMany. State map uses codec composite keys code/panel/build and storage/storageId/panel; unconfirmed attempts do not claim StateToken. Validate recursion same-key rejection permits legitimate different-permission chaining. Pay attention to changed scalar code, batching fast paths, owner/structural query protection and cross-group revisions.\n\nEvidence: accepted-checks.json and V*.log are actual scoped checks; batch-final.log includes final24 cases and newly added cross-group saturation. V1 original101tests25961assertions includes CRM1k/10k plus batch; V6 768related regressions135619assertions; three engines3tests1562assertions each; Arch72/314. V8 PHPStan0 (known optional turbo warning), V9 fresh serial core type99.64%, all209 eligible files reported (three unchanged vendor-plugin-excluded traits). API generator/check and changed PHP Pint/diff GREEN. Behavior checks preceded only type-array-shape/retry-empty guard edits in BatchEvaluation (no normal behavior change); final24 batch cases rerun after those edits. Read evidence independently; GREEN test summaries are not a substitute for code review. Avoid re-reviewing executor discussion or prior native reviews: this snapshot contains only code, contract, diff and checks."}],"_meta":{"screenMode":"headless","promptId":"fbdf4090-faa1-453d-9d52-8f202504cf64"}}
